TITLE: Moving a node between files
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
WIDGET: rows
PLACE: screen
STATEMENT: >>>
Retention class changes by file move; what survives collection; where a backlog item lives.

- A node changes retention class only by moving its file; the UID never changes. Thirteen relocations have held. A dangling relation is fatal; a dangling fingerprint is silent; both are scanned.
> a node changes class only by moving its file; UID never changes; 13 relocations held; dangling Parent = fatal, dangling PARENT_FP = silent, both scanned [WORKS]
- The grid says what survives when a plan is collected — its claims — but not where a surviving claim goes.
[LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-GAP-MEMBERSHIP-AND-COLLECTION-CONTRADICT]
> grid says WHAT survives collection (claims), never WHERE a surviving claim lives [UNADDRESSED]
- Two nodes still say handover freezes the whole plan. A later mechanism narrowed that to the scope handed over.
[LINK: DEC-PLAN-LIFECYCLE-OPEN] [LINK: MECH-PLAN-BEADS-SNAPSHOT] [LINK: MECH-PLAN-CHANGE-KINDS] [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-TYPE-DECISION] [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-TYPE-MECHANISM]
> DEC-PLAN-LIFECYCLE-OPEN STATEMENT and MECH-PLAN-BEADS-SNAPSHOT still say "ingest freezes the plan" [FALLS OUT: MECH-PLAN-CHANGE-KINDS]
- Is a backlog item canon (reviewed) or beads (private)? An unreviewed sketch node sitting on the branch is neither.
[LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-GAP-MEMBERSHIP-AND-COLLECTION-CONTRADICT]
> a backlog item: canon (reviewed) or beads (private)? an unreviewed sketch node on the branch is neither [GAP]
- The beads-migration plan's authoritative source is a rendered artifact plus private markdown, neither in the repo. Which one wins is undecided.
[LINK: DEC-SOURCE-OUT-OF-REPO] [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-TYPE-DECISION]
> beads-migration plan's source = an artifact + private markdown, neither in repo; which wins [OPEN: DEC-SOURCE-OUT-OF-REPO]
- The reason given for putting architecture beside code — 'plans decay and are collected' — is the lean that was since dropped. The placement itself still stands.
[LINK: DEC-ARCH-COLOCATION] [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-TYPE-DECISION]
> DEC-ARCH-COLOCATION's reason ("plans decay and are collected") is the dropped lean; placement stands [OPEN: DEC-ARCH-COLOCATION]
- Scribe's move renames a file outside its load-change-save pipeline, so no joint fires. The library form has no move at all.
> scribe move renames outside load|change|save, so no joint fires; the library form has no move [GAP]
